mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font
                                    face="仿宋">Dr. Chang-rui Chen, is an associate professor of Department of Pharmacology at Fudan University Shanghai Medical College, China. She is a master's degree supervisor, and as a visiting scholar at Harvard University in 2014. She has published dozens of SCI papers and core Chinese journals as the first or corresponding author in international famous journals such as Elife and British Journal of Pharmacology. She has hosted and participated in many national natural science foundation projects. She is a peer-review expert for the National Natural Science Foundation of China, and a reviewer for journals such as Trends in Neurosciences. Main research direction is the study of the role and mechanism of sleep and arousal, and the development of hypnotic drugs. In recent years, she has focused on the role of the paraventricular nucleus of the hypothalamus and the lateral hypothalamus in narcolepsy. These publications have answered the key pathological mechanism of severe somnolence patients. She also focused on insomnia mechanism induced by stress. Dr. Chen had earned PhD at Fudan University in 2007. Since then, she has made great contributions to the teaching of pharmacology to undergraduate and graduate student, and for the MBBS program.</font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
