mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font
                                    face="仿宋">Dr. Zui Zhang, is an associate professor in the department of Pharmacy, School of Basic Medical Sciences of Fudan University. Dr. Zui Zhang has more than 5-years experiences in teaching of undergraduate students, including “functional science experiments” course in the eight-year clinical medicine program, the "Pharmacology" course for medicine, preventive medicine, pediatrics, forensic medicine, and the full-English MBBS class, as well as the integrated course "Respiratory System" of the Strong Foundation Program and the "Pharmacokinetics" course. She participates in the editing work of "Brain-Targeted Drug Delivery" (2019).  Dr. Zui Zhang focuses on the mechanism of brain disease treatment, the transport mode of biological macromolecules under disease conditions, and the active targeted brain strategy. She studies the design of brain-targeted bio-delivery system by “in vivo functionalization”, and construction of targeted drug delivery platform and promoting active targeted nanocarriers from basic to clinical. Her publication includes Proceedings of the national academy of sciences of USA (PNAS), Nature Communications, Nano Letters, J. Control Release and International Journal of Pharmaceutics. She has been authorized for two inventions (2019, 2021). She has presided general project of China Postdoctoral Foundation, National natural youth project, and National natural general project. She has participated in national natural general project and Shanghai Science and Technology Plan project. Honors include Young Researcher Award from Baxter (China) in 2019, the first prize of Youth thesis of 2019 Chinese Pharmaceutical Congress, and Outstanding Postdoctoral Fellow of Fudan University in 2021. </font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
