                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font
                                    face="仿宋">yiqunwang@fudan.edu.cn</font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
                <td width=182 valign=top style="width:109.6500pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font
                                    face="仿宋">Wang Yiqun is an associate professor and a master's supervisor in the Department of Pharmacology at the School of Basic Medicine of Fudan University. Currently, he serves as the secretary of the Sleep Physiology and Pharmacology Committee of the Chinese Sleep Research Society. He has been engaged in research related to neuropharmacology and sleep medicine for a long time. As the first or corresponding author, he has published more than twenty SCI papers in international academic journals such as Nat Commun, Prog Neurobiol, Adv Healthc Mater, CNS Neurosci Ther, Neuropharmacology, and J Neurochem. He has been responsible for over ten scientific research projects including the National Key Research and Development Program, National Natural Science Foundation of China (both regular and youth projects), and Shanghai Natural Science Foundation. He also teaches professional compulsory courses such as "Pharmacology" and "Functional Subject Experiments" for clinical medicine students of eight-year and five-year programs, as well as graduate courses such as "Advanced Pharmacology Advances" for postgraduate students. He has participated in the compilation of textbooks such as "Chart Pharmacology" published by People's Medical Publishing House and "Pharmacology" published by Fudan University Press. He has guided more than ten students to obtain projects such as Shugong Scholar, Zhengyi Scholar, Xiyuan Plan, and Qiangdong Plan. He has also guided students to win the Best Innovation Award at the First Student Practice and Innovation Forum of the School of Basic Medicine of Fudan University. He has received the "Science and Innovation Action" Excellent Instructor Award from the Communist Youth League Committee of Fudan University. He has won awards in the Young Teacher Teaching Competition of the School of Basic Medicine of Fudan University twice.</font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
